# The k8s half of the SECOND tenant of the cross-tenant security fixture: a
# namespace and nothing else. The second tenant deliberately brings no
# WorkerPool, so its actors can only be placed on the pool tenant-pool.yaml.tmpl
# deploys in the first tenant's namespace. That is what puts both tenants on one
# worker; see tenant-pool.yaml.tmpl for why co-residency is the point.
#
# The namespace exists even though no pool runs in it: an atespace's k8s
# namespace is where its namespaced objects (network policies among them) are
# reconciled, so the tenant is only realistic with one.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: ate-e2e${FIXTURE_SUFFIX}
